meta {
  name: Convert Quotation to Order
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "ORDER",
    "orderDate": "2026-07-09",
    "orderType": "WALK_IN",
    "billingType": "CASH_CLIENT",
    "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
    "sourceQuotationId": "{{quotationId}}",
    "items": [
      {
        "branchLabTestId": "{{branchLabTestId}}"
      }
    ],
    "payments": [
      {
        "totalAmount": 500,
        "netAmount": 500,
        "payableAmount": 500,
        "paidAmount": 500,
        "paymentMode": "CASH"
      }
    ]
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.id) bru.setEnvVar("orderId", data.id);
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });
  test("new order links back to the source quotation", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().data.status).to.equal("ORDER");
    expect(res.getBody().data.sourceQuotationId).to.equal(bru.getEnvVar("quotationId"));
  });
}

docs {
  Convert a quotation into a real order — the backend behaviour behind the
  Quotations screen's "Convert to Order" action. This is an ordinary
  `POST /orders` that additionally carries `sourceQuotationId` (the id of the
  source `QUOTE` order). Set `{{quotationId}}` to a DRAFT quotation created
  earlier (e.g. via "Create Order" with `status = QUOTE`).

  What the `sourceQuotationId` link does:

  - When present **and** the new order is finalized (any `status` other than
    `QUOTE` — i.e. `ORDER`, `DRAFT`, or `APPOINTMENT`), the source quote is
    validated (must exist in the tenant and be a quotation — else 422
    `SOURCE_QUOTATION_INVALID`) and its `quotationStatus` is flipped to
    `CONVERTED` **inside the same transaction** that creates the order. So if the
    create fails for any reason (billing rules, overpayment, slot full, …) the
    quote is **not** marked converted — it is all-or-nothing.
  - The source quote keeps `status = QUOTE` (only its `quotationStatus` changes),
    so it stays visible on the Quotations screen (`GET /orders?isQuotation=true`)
    now flagged `CONVERTED`.
  - Ignored on a plain quote save (`status = QUOTE`) — that path is the
    Create/Update Quote and "Save and Close" flows, which never convert.

  Reverse link: quote list rows (`GET /orders?isQuotation=true`) expose the order
  a quote was converted into via `convertedOrderId` / `convertedOrderCode`
  (the latter prefers the user-facing external id, else the order code), driving
  the "View Order" action on a converted quotation.

  See "Create Order" for the full body reference (all other fields behave
  identically).
}
